# Football Intro venues (s3.1.5, renamed + 96×48 only in s3.1.11)

Resume: `@football-intro$` / `@all-stars$`.

**Name (s3.1.11):** visible name is **Football Intro** everywhere (template `name`, help titles in 11 languages, intent label, checkout error, composer eyebrow). Old phrasing still finds it: `searchAliases` + tags keep `zebbies all star(s)`, `all stars`. Template id stays `zebbiesFootballTeamIntro` (old orders, rules, and diagnostics key on it).

It is offered at:

| Venue | Location id |
|---|---|
| Zebbies Garden DC | `zebbies-garden-washington-dc` |
| Heist Washington DC | `heist-washington-dc` (also in its restricted `templates` list) |
| Aurelia (QA demo club) | `temp-democlub-1` |

Three places must agree when the list changes:

1. `shared-data.js` → `SHOUTOUT_TEMPLATES.zebbiesFootballTeamIntro.venueIds` (composer offering; `patron-app.js` `footballIntroAllowedHere()` reads it).
2. `functions/commerce-functions.js` → `FOOTBALL_TEAM_INTRO_LOCATION_IDS` (server gate in `normalizeCheckoutPayload` + `describeOrder`; order keeps the requested club). Redeploy `createFloqrCheckoutSession`.
3. Restricted venues (`restrictTemplatesToLocationSet`) also list the id in their `templates`.

**96×48 only (s3.1.11, owner request):** `Is96x48:1, Is64x48:0, Is64x32:0`, `screenFormatIds` / `preferredFormatIds` = `['led-96x48']`. Same for Tengo muchos dólares (`heistVaultDollars` + alias `heistRedLux`). Checkout forces `screenFormatId:"led-96x48"` via `LED_96X48_ONLY_TEMPLATE_IDS` (Heist art used to default to `led-64x32`). All three venues have a 96×48 board (Heist: primary 96×48, secondary 64×32 → these play on `display.html` only).

Headline default and finale label are `{BRAND} FOOTBALL INTRO` from the venue `brandName` (composer `footballIntroDefaultMain()`, board `allStarsLabel` in `display-app.js`; variable name kept).

Tests: `functions/football-intro-venues.test.js`.
